{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793973112,"nonce":"/OHl4NCJ6BL7AgpiTysWYAtoQYQ=","message":"Fixed in eeda0864. try_as_simple_selector no longer stores an id rule with :checked or :disabled as a simple pointer-state rule; they are complex rules matched on the element's checked and disabled attributes (has_state() counts pointer-driven states only, so they are base complex rules), which orders them against the widgets' class rules by specificity and re-evaluates them as the attribute changes. The checkbox golden now records #cb:checked (#228844) on a checked box and #cb:disabled on a disabled one; three parser/table tests that asserted the old storage were updated. Remaining difference from a browser is filed separately.","files":null}]}